course: dictionary
lesson: 5793
title: Learning a word from clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing you have never seen. Context can paint a picture. «Macaws are the biggest parrots» tells you a macaw is a kind of parrot, and that it is big.
explain: Look for clues about what the thing looks like, what it does, or where it lives. «A parrot's hooked beak and strong jaw crack hard nuts» tells you a macaw has a strong, hooked beak. «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America» tells you where to find one.
explain: Put your clues together, then check. Swap your meaning into the sentence. Does it still make sense? A macaw is a large, colourful parrot from the rainforest, and every sentence fits that picture.
fact: A macaw is a large parrot with a long tail and a strong, curved beak.
fact: Macaws have very bright feathers, such as red, blue, yellow and green.
fact: Macaws come from the rainforests of Central and South America.
fact: «Macaws are the biggest parrots», and a hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.
fact: Macaws crack hard nuts with their beaks, and many kinds are endangered because of forest loss and the illegal pet trade.
exercise: «Macaws are the biggest parrots.» What is a macaw? | *A large parrot | A type of tree | A small fish | A kind of rock
exercise: «A parrot's hooked beak and strong jaw crack hard nuts and seeds.» What is a macaw's beak like? | Small and round | *Hooked and strong | Long and thin like a straw | Soft and flat
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Scarlet macaws fly in pairs that stay together for many years.» that tells you macaws live with a partner. | years | fly | *pairs | scarlet
test: Which colours can a macaw's feathers be? | Black and white only | *Red, blue, yellow and green | Purple only | Brown and grey only
test: «Macaws can copy sounds and some words.» What does this tell you about a macaw? | It is a plant that grows in the forest | It never makes any sound at all | *It can copy sounds it hears | It only sings in the morning
exam: Read the clue: «A macaw's beak cracks palm nuts so hard that people need a hammer.» What does this tell you about a macaw's beak? | *It is very strong | It is too small to eat anything | It is very soft | It is made of paper
